proposed_change:
Factor inventory.js useOrEquip into an exported activateItem(guid, {cell}) on window.__inventory. It should:
- apply the 0.2 s throttle;
- resolve the row from playerInventory;
- if owned and not wielded and wieldable (weapon/held/shield/ammo locations, or Caster type), do the existing wield path (executeItemAction op 'wield', which reaches the wasm WieldFromPack swap); if it has armour/clothing/jewellery locations that are not worn, do the same for 'wear';
- if TinkeringTool, call __openSalvagePanel;
- else if classifyUse().needsTarget, call __useTargeting.begin;
- else useObject.
Call it from hotbar.js fireSlot (new decideFireAction kind 'activateItem' for item bindings), app/hud_panels.js Use button and radial-menu 'Use'.
Optional follow-up (wasm): add combatUse and the WieldOnUse/WieldLeft bits to InventoryItem, or a Rust classifyPrimaryUse(guid) port of DetermineUseResult in holtburger-world context.rs, so the JS rule matches retail exactly instead of inferring from validLocations.

